# PixelBoats Fish Water Ecology Skill

## Goal

Integrate the fish-water prototype into PixelBoats as a real gameplay/ecology system, not as a one-off visual gag.

The feature should add:

- multiple drifting schools of fish in the world map;
- underwater/surface/breach/skim/submerge fish behaviour;
- water ripples, splashes, surface impulses, and debug-box visibility;
- fish that can rarely jump onto the player boat and grant food;
- seagull flocks that discover and exploit fish schools;
- sharks that react to nearby schools, chum/captures, and dense biomass;
- a giant fish net perk/item for harvesting multiple fish in open ocean.

This skill must preserve the PixelBoats P0 rule: do not destabilize start/death state, boat scale/collision, render ordering, item density, rocks/sandbars, wake readability, or WebGL2 performance while adding content.

## When To Use

Use this skill for:

- fish school system planning or implementation;
- water ripple/splash integration from fish events;
- fish catch / food reward mechanics;
- seagull and shark ecology around fish schools;
- giant net perk / AoE capture logic;
- fish-water debug scene, tuning panel, and settings schema;
- turning the HTML fish-water prototype into PixelBoats app modules;
- writing prompts for Trae/Codex/GPT to implement this feature.

Do **not** use this skill for:

- unrelated UI/HUD redesigns;
- full map editor/Wake Lab implementation;
- broad water shader rewrites before P0 is visually stable;
- flamingo/easter-egg/sprite-sheet work;
- bypassing existing boat physics, collision, or render order rules.

